        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: дети",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "дети (déti) — \"children\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "дети (déti) is the plural of дитя, \"a child\", from Proto-Slavic dětę, děti — inherited. Vasmer traces it to the PIE root dʰeh₁(i)-, \"to suckle\", the root of доить, \"to milk\": a child is one who is nursed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
