          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ребёнок (rebyónok) — \"a child\". One child; дети (déti) is the plural."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ребёнок (rebyónok) grew from Old Russian робя, \"child\", Proto-Slavic orbę, with a diminutive ending; роб- became реб- by an old vowel assimilation (Vasmer). The same root gave раб, \"slave\", and Vasmer lists Latin orbus, \"bereaved\", and Greek orphanós, \"orphan\", as cousins."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
