          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "внучка (vnúchka) is внук (vnuk), \"grandson\", with -ка, which makes the female word; к turns to ч before it, as in рука, \"hand\", and ручка, \"a little hand; a pen\". Vasmer traces внук (vnuk) to Proto-Slavic vŭnukŭ and tentatively links it with an old nursery word for an elder, kept in Latin anus, \"old woman\"."
